===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)mer-|id=remember}}
From {{der|en|xno|memorie}}, {{der|en|fro|memoire}} etc., from {{der|en|la|memoria||the faculty of remembering, remembrance, memory, a historical account}}, from {{m|la|memor||mindful, remembering}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)mer-}} (to remember), related to {{cog|grc|μνήμη||memory}} {{m|grc|μέρμερος||anxious}}, {{m|grc|μέριμνα||care, thought}}, {{cog|ang|ġemimor||mindful, remembering}}. More at {{l|en|mimmer}}. {{doublet|en|memoir|memoria}}. Displaced native {{ncog|ang|myne}} (whence {{cog|en|min}}) and {{ncog|ang|ġemynd}}, which took on a different meaning as  modern {{m|en|mind}}.

